    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "**DETACHED BUNGLAOW IN ONE OF COUNTY KILDARE'S MOST SOUGHT AFTER LOCATIONS**\r\n\r\nDowling Property is delighted to present to the market this truly rare occasion to acquire a delightful detached home, in quite simply one of County Kildare’s most sought after locations. Standing on a c.0.6 acre site nestled between Brannockstown, Naas and Ballymore Eustace, this superb property is located on a quiet local access road in the heart of the countryside.\r\n\r\nThis charming, 3 bedroom detached bungalow is approached via a wonderful driveway flanked by a mature Beech hedging which leads you to the perfectly positioned property in the centre of the site allowing for generous sized gardens to front and rear. Features include 3 double bedrooms (master en-suite), large utility room, oil heating with open fire and double glazed windows.\r\n\r\nThe mature gardens are a real highlight and have been well maintained over the years by its original owners from new. The south facing rear enjoys rolling countryside views over some of the counties finest lands. This fine property also benefits from extensive road frontage. There is endless potential for extending and reconfiguration for the new owners (S.T.P.P.) as there is space around all corners of the property. With it’s first class location and magical site we must now advise on early viewings of this chain free sale, as opportunities like this are truly rare. One Not To Be Missed!!\r\n\r\nThe accommodation, which is well laid out, consists of entrance hallway, sitting room, kitchen/dining room, utility, 3 double bedrooms (master en-suite) and family bathroom.\r\n\r\nAll amenities can be found close by in Ballymore Eustace/Naas or Kilcullen including a selection of top class primary and secondary school. Naas is home to large multi-national shops including Tesco, Dunnes, Lidl and Aldi and has direct access to M7."
      },
